BARNSTABLE HIGH SCHOOL PITCH
- Can we do a poetry slam, which days?
- I want there to be two slams, one real one in the Knight for the word nerds and the film production one in the big auditorium that's just an efficient film shoot

MELODY TENT PITCH
- Can we intersect with a day while the tent is up during a time at which there is no show
- we just need to get a few shots of footage of the parade entering and the circus starting, there is not a literal eternal circus at the end of days. just a couple of hours top to bottom.
- wink wink fellow circus folk wink wink

CAPE COD TIMES PITCH
- do you want to be involved in the show from start to finish or is the surprise ending okay
- also if you're not comfortable with doing all the facial reactions, we have a professional mime on standby that is versed in the materials we can use as a stunt double

BARNSTABLE POLICE DEPARTMENT
- just a heads up that we'll obey all side walks and traffic crossings on the parade path but if we can get the street shut down that would be great

! director's note: the entire premise is a ploy to do a free show at the melody tent for the groundlings so the physical venues and the entire cast are fixed realities for this plot to work at all

! producer's note: we do need a budget large enough to tear down Sturgis Charter School to re-implement an even larger Amusment Center and I need Paulio's original recipe because the pizza has not been as good since the first year they opened back when I got the employee discount and utilized it religiously and I need that to be a staple for this immersive experience to be a self-sustaining self-fulfilling prophecy

! note to investors: this is a legacy initiative for you to leave a mark on restoring our Presidential Historical District. The project will re-vitalize our downtown that is crucial to the tourism industry that drives our local economy. we now have the data to show the bowling alley was a better driver for bringing people from all over the world to our main street compared to every other Main Street U.S.A. in comparison to a school that's objectively under performing the public school system after this successful production architected by a BHS alumnus.

! note to sturgis: no offense, but you could have literally built anywhere-- why did you choose to destroy the economic capital of our region? which school taught you to behave like that?

